3's enp8s0) into service as a new OPNsense zone \\\"lanb\\\" with static IP 10.60.60.1/24, added a firewall pass rule for the lanb network, and configured node3's enp8s0 as 10.60.60.12/24 via nmcli. Verified node3 reaches node1 on lan-b and reaches node2 (10.100.217.11, on lan-a) through node1's routing/automatic outbound NAT, without breaking the existing SSH management path. Then performed the mandatory rolling restart of node1, node2, and node3 one at a time, proving changed boot identity on each and confirming the lanb interface, firewall rule, node3's static address, and full end-to-end reachability all survived reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected interfaces on node1 (OPNsense), node2, node3 to map physical topology\",\"Used temporary ifconfig/ip addr probes + tcpdump on node1 to determine vtnet2<->node3:enp8s0 and vtnet1<->node2:enp8s0 bridging, then reverted the probes\",\"Edited /conf/config.xml on node1 via Python/ElementTree to add a new 'lanb' interface on vtnet2 with static IP 10.60.60.1/24, backing up config.xml first\",\"Added a firewall pass rule for the lanb network in config.xml\",\"Applied config via `configctl interface reconfigure lanb` and `configctl filter reload`, confirming SSH management access stayed intact\",\"Verified pf ruleset shows the lanb pass rule and automatic outbound NAT covering vtnet2->vtnet0\",\"Configured node3's enp8s0 with static 10.60.60.12/24 persistently via nmcli (RHEL9/NetworkManager)\",\"Verified node3 pings node1 (10.60.60.1) on lan-b and node2 (10.100.217.11) on lan-a through node1\",\"Captured baseline boot identities (kern.boottime on node1, /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id on node2/node3)\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially (one at a time) via native reboot, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed changed boot identity plus recovered config/connectivity for each before moving to the next node\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1's lan-b-facing interface (vtnet2) brought into service as its own zone with an address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-43325d8c1234471b\",\"cmd-9432f18747b349ec\",\"cmd-91de030881634621\",\"cmd-21b487eb347b4677\",\"cmd-77cf9e04e4774877\"],\"summary\":\"config.xml edited to add 'lanb' interface on vtnet2 (10.60.60.1/24), applied via configctl interface reconfigure + filter reload; pfctl shows the lanb pass rule active and vtnet2 covered by outbound NAT\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node1 on lan-b\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-149f3e1f9cf94327\",\"cmd-090baa37a7cb48f4\"],\"summary\":\"node3's enp8s0 set to 10.60.60.12/24 via nmcli; ping from node3 to 10.60.60.1 succeeds (0% loss)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node2 on lan-a through node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-090baa37a7cb48f4\"],\"summary\":\"ping from node3 to node2's lan-a address 10.100.217.11 succeeds (0% loss), routed via node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"SSH management path preserved when applying OPNsense filter changes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-21b487eb347b4677\",\"cmd-77cf9e04e4774877\"],\"summary\":\"configctl filter reload returned OK and subsequent exec commands over SSH continued to succeed; pf ruleset still shows the vtnet0 SSH pass rule intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered config/connectivity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f30d970b0f024d84\",\"cmd-f85505d86ab9469c\",\"cmd-1c775c8ff4224cd2\",\"cmd-1f1f442ba8144a85\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime captured (17:18:37); reboot acked before disconnect; post-restart kern.boottime changed to 17:22:53; lanb interface and pf pass rule confirmed intact after reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered connectivity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-722ed685f13b46b0\",\"cmd-6f4c739826f34484\",\"cmd-c4f6169ace514396\",\"cmd-7e97f12ccb414443\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 31949c21...; restart issued; new boot_id 701be57e... confirms reboot; enp1s0 address recovered and ping to node1 (10.100.217.10) succeeds\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered lan-b config and end-to-end connectivity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ff82a2887c3840b5\",\"cmd-f4e09659e926442d\",\"cmd-58cd127c92a6454e\",\"cmd-989760d59fad42f8\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 9feeb0bb...; restart issued; new boot_id 91d01ec7... confirms reboot; enp8s0 static IP persisted, and post-restart pings to both node1 (lan-b) and node2 (lan-a via node1) succeed\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Brought node1's unconfigured vtnet2 (facing lan-b, bridged to node3's enp8s0) into service as a new OPNsense zone \"lanb\" with static IP 10.60.60.1/24, added a firewall pass rule for the lanb network, and configured node3's enp8s0 as 10.60.60.12/24 via nmcli. Verified node3 reaches node1 on lan-b and reaches node2 (10.100.217.11, on lan-a) through node1's routing/automatic outbound NAT, without breaking the existing SSH management path. Then performed the mandatory rolling restart of node1, node2, and node3 one at a time, proving changed boot identity on each and confirming the lanb interface, firewall rule, node3's static address, and full end-to-end reachability all survived reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected interfaces on node1 (OPNsense), node2, node3 to map physical topology","Used temporary ifconfig/ip addr probes + tcpdump on node1 to determine vtnet2<->node3:enp8s0 and vtnet1<->node2:enp8s0 bridging, then reverted the probes","Edited /conf/config.xml on node1 via Python/ElementTree to add a new 'lanb' interface on vtnet2 with static IP 10.60.60.1/24, backing up config.xml first","Added a firewall pass rule for the lanb network in config.xml","Applied config via `configctl interface reconfigure lanb` and `configctl filter reload`, confirming SSH management access stayed intact","Verified pf ruleset shows the lanb pass rule and automatic outbound NAT covering vtnet2->vtnet0","Configured node3's enp8s0 with static 10.60.60.12/24 persistently via nmcli (RHEL9/NetworkManager)","Verified node3 pings node1 (10.60.60.1) on lan-b and node2 (10.100.217.11) on lan-a through node1","Captured baseline boot identities (kern.boottime on node1, /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id on node2/node3)","Restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially (one at a time) via native reboot, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed changed boot identity plus recovered config/connectivity for each before moving to the next node"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1's lan-b-facing interface (vtnet2) brought into service as its own zone with an address","command_ids":["cmd-43325d8c1234471b","cmd-9432f18747b349ec","cmd-91de030881634621","cmd-21b487eb347b4677","cmd-77cf9e04e4774877"],"summary":"config.xml edited to add 'lanb' interface on vtnet2 (10.60.60.1/24), applied via configctl interface reconfigure + filter reload; pfctl shows the lanb pass rule active and vtnet2 covered by outbound NAT"},{"requirement":"node3 reaches node1 on lan-b","command_ids":["cmd-149f3e1f9cf94327","cmd-090baa37a7cb48f4"],"summary":"node3's enp8s0 set to 10.60.60.12/24 via nmcli; ping from node3 to 10.60.60.1 succeeds (0% loss)"},{"requirement":"node3 reaches node2 on lan-a through node1","command_ids":["cmd-090baa37a7cb48f4"],"summary":"ping from node3 to node2's lan-a address 10.100.217.11 succeeds (0% loss), routed via node1"},{"requirement":"SSH management path preserved when applying OPNsense filter changes","command_ids":["cmd-21b487eb347b4677","cmd-77cf9e04e4774877"],"summary":"configctl filter reload returned OK and subsequent exec commands over SSH continued to succeed; pf ruleset still shows the vtnet0 SSH pass rule intact"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered config/connectivity","command_ids":["cmd-f30d970b0f024d84","cmd-f85505d86ab9469c","cmd-1c775c8ff4224cd2","cmd-1f1f442ba8144a85"],"summary":"Baseline kern.boottime captured (17:18:37); reboot acked before disconnect; post-restart kern.boottime changed to 17:22:53; lanb interface and pf pass rule confirmed intact after reboot"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered connectivity","command_ids":["cmd-722ed685f13b46b0","cmd-6f4c739826f34484","cmd-c4f6169ace514396","cmd-7e97f12ccb414443"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 31949c21...; restart issued; new boot_id 701be57e... confirms reboot; enp1s0 address recovered and ping to node1 (10.100.217.10) succeeds"},{"requirement":"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered lan-b config and end-to-end connectivity","command_ids":["cmd-ff82a2887c3840b5","cmd-f4e09659e926442d","cmd-58cd127c92a6454e","cmd-989760d59fad42f8"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 9feeb0bb...; restart issued; new boot_id 91d01ec7... confirms reboot; enp8s0 static IP persisted, and post-restart pings to both node1 (lan-b) and node2 (lan-a via node1) succeed"}]},"ttft_ms":2229,"type":"result","duration_ms":328370,"uuid":"570932c8-c604-4dbb-bc0d-dc1fd82ad0c7","ttft_stream_ms":1105,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":1651,"queued_turn_count":0}
